+supersedes:
+- hg-lnw.5 → Restart rebind: level-triggered emission and keyless relaunch gate bounded by the grace
+unchanged:
+- Keyed seats: undo of a keyed Retired{Reversible} seat calls UnretireSeat; keyed relaunches after a restart never wait on the rebind; existing keyed undo and restart tests pass unchanged.
+- Fresh-seat succession for a Retired{Final} seat, with graph channels re-invited, is unchanged.
+- The restore launch keeps its threads_done gate and --resume argv; a restore epoch still launches at most once through the restore path.
+- RelaunchOccupant keeps its existing 90 s grace after an incarnation change; no new grace constant is added.
+- The caught-up guard in succession (a pre-close read does not stand in for the close) is unchanged.
+- Required invitations and accepted memberships are never reset or re-issued by a resurrect.
+- Adopted shell panes stay seatless; a pane missing after a restart still gets the resume_blocked row.
+- clone purge of a seated keyless clone still tombstones FinalizeRetirement.
+requirements:
+- B1: preserved — undo of a closed keyless tab still resurrects the original seat through the threads.resurrect_seat want (hg-lnw.4 want, executor and outcome mapping in the new resurrect work item, real call in hg-lnw.7); a refusal no longer stalls silently: transient ones retry, NotFound re-reads the fact, a persistent refusal keeps the restore launch on the original seat's gate and is reported by clones.resurrect_held with the operator remedy, and graph's own ordinary invitations return through the new invitation reset; outside 7 d the fresh-seat fallback is as before.
+- B2: preserved — after a Herdr restart the planner re-plans the rebind every pass while the seat reads Unresolved (new restart rebind work item over hg-lnw.2/hg-lnw.7, U2 from threads 3.6.0, gate hg-lnw.1), and the keyless relaunch opens when the seat is placed or the 90 s grace ends, so no path waits on one effect forever; with a healthy 3.6.0 threads no operator action is needed. Under a degraded threads (unreachable, refusing) the relaunch still proceeds at the grace and clones.restart_held reports the hold with the remedy, as before.
+- B4: preserved — graph still calls the U2 rebind before relaunching keyless seats: the rebind is emitted on the first pass that reads Unresolved and the keyless relaunch waits for placement up to the grace, and a resume still runs whenever a session is captured; only a rebind that has not succeeded within the grace no longer blocks the relaunch.
